{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner ruling on pass capacity for fc2548ae. It answers the open capacity point (7bb58c3b, 53279be5, cde4b4a3) and the options in 10f9df62.\n\n1. Acceptance is a cold fit, measured. Under unchanged ARCHIVE_BOUNDS, with no warm memory:\n- the installed Grow test passes with its assertions unchanged, except one: ruling 63a9216f makes the migration pass archive no entries, so in legacy cases the first-pass entry assertions move to the first native pass;\n- in the 37-pass and 6-pass fixtures, every native pass after migration plans at least one entry;\n- the Native300 drain completes.\nThe note gives the measured maximum nodes and metadata per pass and the margin to 64 nodes and 4 MiB. No universal capacity claim is needed.\n\n2. Means. A warm memo alone does not meet point 1, because every cold or restarted pass still pays full validation; do not build it in this head. Native state that was written through the private CAS after full validation can be trusted on a later pass by an exact-bytes digest check against the row that records it, instead of a second walk of its trees. Full validation stays for the migration pass, for state without a recorded digest and after any mismatch. Use this check, the through-bound work profile (1d451c03) or the writer witness, whichever meets point 1 with the smallest change. No cap changes.\n\n3. If point 1 cannot be met under unchanged caps, report the measured shortfall on each axis before the review request. The planner then chooses between a cap change and a smaller pass.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}